  "reason": "ot_hbm_su_programme_root5 is itself the root register stage of the SU programme (root + cluster head pin stage): every output is a register output (r_start/r_len/r_we/r_bank/r_row/r_data/fault), start/length land on the SDLY 2 delay registers, cfg_* on the root register (cfg_bank through the per-part range compare / base subtract, as root_h), p_fault on the fault OR register, rst_n drives only ot_rst_relay (release +3, as the r5 leaves). A kit flop stage would add an edge the start-advance contract does not price."
 },
 "children": [],
 "inter": [],
 "clock": "cts",
 "structural_change": "NEW master (HBM-RTL5 2026-10-18): root register su_pgr for the d4g GEN1 per-column programme clusters ot_hbm_su_programme_pslice_c5 (pgp_<q>; NATIVE-FIX3/pgs leaves pgcol_s r5 / pghead r5). ot_hbm_su_programme_root_h5 = ot_hbm_su_programme_root5 PARTS 4, SMACROS 4 x 320 (bank = 320 part + 32 column + local), SDLY 2 (start/length +2 edges so the clusters' +2 configuration edges stay host-invisible: write-on-start pairing and config-before-start rules = r4), RRLY 1 (rst_n -> ot_rst_relay, root releases with the clusters, +3). Every programme output is the r4 output 2 edges later (whole-path bench tb_hbm_su_programme_root5 vs root_h + 4 x pslice_q4). Same ports/outline/pin faces as hbm_su_pgroot_1017 (closed root_h kept for the d4f/GEN0 composition).",
